        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Wall outlet, base switch, safety key, a moment for the console,
            then start.</strong> On most home treadmills the power switch is at the front of the
            base near the cord, not on the console, and the safety key has to be in place before
            the belt will run.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the screen stays dark, check the key, the switch, the reset button and the outlet
            before suspecting a fault, and give a touchscreen time to boot or update. For anything
            beyond that, our guide to a
            <a href="/treadmill-wont-turn-on/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">treadmill that will not turn on</a>
